{
  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_008: scgpt+resnet50+avgpool+weighted → 52.5% acc, 4.42 GPU hrs), the evidence is sparse and the biggest uncertainty is whether the image encoder is a bottleneck. Config_007 changes exactly one variable from the baseline—upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L—while keeping scgpt, avgpool, and weighted fusion identical. This gives a clean A/B comparison to isolate the image-encoder contribution. ViT-L is substantially more expressive than ResNet50, so the potential accuracy upside is large; if it helps, the image branch is a key lever and we can exploit it further; if it doesn't, we rule out the image encoder and redirect effort toward RNA encoding, aggregation, or fusion. Expected cost is moderate-to-high (~7–9 GPU hrs) due to the larger ViT-L backbone, but with 8 experiments remaining the budget can absorb one expensive high-information experiment. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it targets the single highest-impact design axis with minimal confounding."
}

